1
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:14,810
Long, long ago, God's people, the Israelites, lived in Egypt. The king of Egypt, Pharaoh, made them slaves. Every day they made bricks and carried bricks, until their backs ached.

2
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:21,040
Faster! Faster! Not one brick less today! Hmph!

3
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:28,260
Oh God... can you hear us crying? Please, please save us!

4
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:39,870
Far away in the wilderness lived an old shepherd named Moses. He grew up in Pharaoh's palace when he was young, but now his beard was white.

5
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:50,670
Hm? That bush is on fire... but it isn't burning up! I'll go and have a look.

6
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:55,490
Moses! Moses!

7
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:58,250
I... I'm here!

8
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:08,180
I have seen my people suffering in Egypt, and I have heard them crying. Now go to Pharaoh, and bring my people out of Egypt.

9
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:20,690
Me? Who am I?... And I'm no good at talking. When I speak, I... I get all mixed up.

10
00:01:21,490 --> 00:01:25,560
What is that in your hand? Throw it on the ground.

11
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:29,770
Whoa! A snake! A snake!

12
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:37,560
Don't be afraid. Take it by the tail. I will be with you, and I will teach you what to say.

13
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:42,800
All right... I'll go!

14
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:52,590
Pharaoh! This is what God says: Let my people go!

15
00:01:53,190 --> 00:02:01,690
Ha ha ha! God? Which god? Never heard of him! No! I won't let them go!

16
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:12,420
So God sent trouble after trouble: the river turned red, frogs hopped everywhere, then came flies, and hail...

17
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:20,750
Ribbit?... Aaah! A frog! Get it off, get it off! All right, all right, you can go!

18
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:25,840
But as soon as the frogs were gone, Pharaoh changed his mind.

19
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:30,430
Heh heh... changed my mind!

20
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:42,350
At last God said one more trouble would come, the worst of all. He told his people to put a mark on their doors and stay inside that night, and they would be safe.

21
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:49,950
Everyone, eat up! Shoes on, bags packed! Tonight we're leaving!

22
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:56,870
Go... just go! Take your sheep and go, all of you!

23
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:02,680
We're free!

24
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:09,360
God went ahead of them: a pillar of cloud by day, and a pillar of fire by night.

25
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:18,290
Wait! They've all gone... then who's going to make my bricks? My chariot! After them!

26
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:24,510
Moses! The sea is in front of us, and Pharaoh's chariots are behind us... what do we do?

27
00:03:25,110 --> 00:03:30,190
Don't be afraid! Stand still, and watch how God will save us!

28
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:43,410
Moses stretched out his staff over the sea. God sent a strong wind that blew all night, and whoosh! The water split apart, and there was a dry path right through the middle!

29
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:50,020
Wow... the water is standing up like two walls! Come on, everyone, let's go!

30
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:07,800
Charge! Huh? My wheel! Hey, hey, hey... waaah!

31
00:04:10,090 --> 00:04:18,570
The water came rushing back, and Pharaoh's chariots could not follow any more. God's people were safe on the other side of the sea!

32
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:23,470
Ah... ah... ACHOO!

33
00:04:25,670 --> 00:04:33,460
Sing to the Lord, sing! He has won the victory! Horse and chariot, he threw into the sea!

34
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:35,990
Sing to the Lord! Sing!

35
00:04:37,670 --> 00:04:42,070
God heard us when we cried, and he led us all the way.

36
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:49,190
When you're scared, you can pray to God too. He hears you, and he'll show you the way!
